# Root property of the full-kernel quotient at odd levels

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelIsRootAt_of_odd`
(`6fe3f97f-7a7c-504d-a72b-329e539e4016`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `e394d22c-2b9d-59c4-9997-70325fbc01f0`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a positive natural number which is odd. The assertion is the predicate
`FullKernelIsRootAt N`, namely: for every Weierstrass curve $W$ over the field $H$ of Hahn series
with rational exponents and coefficients in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which is elliptic, every point
$Q$ of the affine model of $W$ whose additive order is exactly $N$, under the hypothesis $h_\Delta$
that the discriminant of the curve $W.\mathrm{fullKernelQuotient}\,Q\,N$ is nonzero (so that this
curve is itself elliptic, its discriminant being a unit), and for every datum `data` of type
[`ModularCurve.ModularPolynomialData N`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L215) — that is, a polynomial
$\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ which is monic, has natural degree equal to $\psi(N)$ (the Dedekind
$\psi$-function of $N$), and satisfies $\Phi$ evaluated at `evalAtJ` and `jqN N` equal to zero — the
one-variable polynomial over $H$ obtained from $\Phi$ by mapping each coefficient through evaluation
of its integer polynomial at $j(W)$ has the $j$-invariant of $W.\mathrm{fullKernelQuotient}\,Q\,N$
as a root. Here $W.\mathrm{fullKernelQuotient}\,Q\,N$ is the Weierstrass curve produced by Vélu's
construction `veluQuotientOfSums` from the sums of $G_x(P)$ and of $x_P G_x(P) - y_P G_y(P)$ over
the set `W.oddOrderSummingSet Q (N - 1)`.

This is the level-$N$ modular equation $\Phi_N\bigl(j(W), j(W/\langle Q\rangle)\bigr) = 0$ for the
Vélu quotient of an elliptic curve by the cyclic group generated by a point of exact order $N$,
stated over the Hahn-series field used for the Tate curve. It is the odd-level case of the root
property and feeds into
[`ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelIsRootAt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelIsRootAt).

